The SkillSync project has been rewritten from Dynamic/FastAPI/HTML into a React (Vite + TypeScript) application while preserving all core features, algorithmic balancing models, and business logic.
Ported Features
Authentication & User Switching:
Secure login and registration with sample credentials (coordinator@skillsync.test, student1@skillsync.test, password Demo@1234).
Interactive demo role/account switcher in the header to navigate between coordinator and student experiences.
Scoring & Evaluation Algorithm:
Exact implementation of skillScore, generalScore, competitionFit, and leadershipScore.
Comprehensive team balancer implementing multi-objective greedy allocation and iterative swap search across tolerance constraints, leadership allocation, and partner preferences (prefer / avoid).
Coordinator Dashboard:
Competition creation with customizable track types and weighted skill requirements.
Lifecycle management: draft publishing, registration closing, and applicant auditing.
Team generation with candidate option tabs, fairness tolerance checks, and team averages bar charts.
Team finalization and Monte Carlo fairness simulation report benchmarked against 300 random trials.
CSV export of finalized team rosters and member scores.
Student Dashboard:
General score display and top skills progress bars.
Chart.js radar chart visualization for skill strength distribution.
Interactive profile and skill rating editor (proficiency and experience scores).
Competition discovery with real-time eligibility checks, volunteer leadership checkbox, and application submission.
Teammate wish management (selecting up to 3 peers to prefer or avoid).
Team Workspace:
Sprint progress indicator and planned member workload bar chart.
Milestone tracking with overdue notices and completion toggles.
3-column Kanban board (To do, In progress, Done) with role-based task movement and assignment.
Persistence & Data Layer
Client-side reactive in-memory and local storage layer initialized with the complete demo dataset (15 technical skills, coordinator Prof. Sharma, 30 students with pre-configured ratings, applications, and teammate preferences).
Full state changes (creating competitions, applying, generating teams, finalizing, managing workspace tasks) persist across sessions.
Known Limitations
Data persistence is browser-local (localStorage); multi-device synchronization is not configured.
